3. Features Implemented
Requirement 1 — Raspberry Pi Health Status Model
Reliable Identification: Inspects /proc/device-tree/model and compatible for Raspberry Pi 5 or bcm2712. Generic ARM devices are not falsely categorized as RPi 5.
Configurable Pilot Thresholds:
CPU temperature: Warning at 75°C, Critical at 80°C.
Undervoltage detection: Active bit 0x1 raises THROTTLED_UNDERVOLTAGE (Critical).
Thermal throttling: Active bit 0x4 raises THROTTLED_THERMAL (Warning).
Preserved NVIDIA thresholds (Jetson Thor 95°C/105°C; Orin Nano 85°C/95°C).
Missing GPU Safety: Raspberry Pi 5 reports VideoCore VII GPU; NVML and tegrastats are safely bypassed and do not trigger false GPU overheating or missing GPU warnings.
Deterministic Precedence: Offline (missed heartbeats) ➔ Critical ➔ Warning ➔ Online.
Requirement 2 — Heartbeat and Switch-Off Counting
Event Classification: Distinguishes between:
CONFIRMED_REBOOT: Detected via changes in /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id across heartbeats.
RESTART_UNEXPECTED: Uptime reset without a recorded graceful shutdown.
AGENT_RESTARTED: Monotonic uptime and identical boot ID across an agent gap.
SHUTDOWN_CLEAN: Trapped and transmitted on SIGTERM/SIGINT.
CONNECTION_INTERRUPTED & DEVICE_OFFLINE: Server-evaluated communication drops.
Deduplication: Buffered historical heartbeats (buffered: true) replayed after an outage update time-series data without triggering duplicate reboot or shutdown events.
Requirement 3 — Hardware Telemetry
Linux-Native Interfaces: Utilizes psutil for per-core CPU and memory; shutil.disk_usage() for root and storage mounts.
Temperature & Throttling: Reads vcgencmd measure_temp and vcgencmd get_throttled (parsing active bits 0x1, 0x2, 0x4, 0x8 and historical bits 0x10000–0x80000).
Resilient Fallback: When vcgencmd is absent (minimal OS installations), falls back automatically to /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp and marks throttling metrics as unavailable without failing the heartbeat cycle.
Requirement 4 — Last-24-Hour Time-Series Data
UTC Preservation: Original device event timestamps (sent_at) are preserved during offline backfilling and never overwritten with server ingestion time.
Storage & Downsampling: Metrics are downsampled into 720 equal time buckets over 24 hours. Unsupported or missing metrics are explicitly stored and returned as JSON null, never falsely reported as 0.
Retention: Periodic background retention prunes data older than retention_days (default 30 days) across metrics, logs, and plain-text archives.
Requirement 5 — Dynamic Device Parameters
Hierarchy: DEFAULT ➔ ORGANIZATION ➔ SCHOOL ➔ DEVICE. More specific valid overrides take precedence.
Validation: Strict range validation on numerical settings (e.g. interval_s 5–3600, log_level DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR/CRITICAL). Invalid settings return 400 Bad Request.
Atomic Persistence: Agent validates version numbers, applies updates safely, and atomically writes the last known valid configuration to last_known_config.json for offline survival.
Requirement 6 — Log Categorization and Collection
Structured JSON Schema: Standardized fields: event_id, device_id, service, category, severity, timestamp, message, attributes, received_at.
Categories: APPLICATION, API, SYNC, SYSTEM, AI, SECURITY, and UPDATE.
Sensitive Data Redaction: Regular expressions redact API keys, tokens, passwords, authorization headers, and private keys with [REDACTED].
Deduplication: event_id primary key prevents duplicate logs during buffer replay.
Requirement 7 — Log-Stop and Inactivity Detection
State Classification: Distinguishes between:
running: Service health check passed and active.
idle: Service health check passed, listening, but no recent log lines produced (normal idle state; no false alarm).
stopped: Service health check failed or systemd unit stopped.
unknown: Agent is offline or check could not be completed.
Requirement 8 — AI Workload Monitoring
Ollama Adapter: Added official adapter polling /api/version and /api/ps for Raspberry Pi 5.
Metrics Collected: Active loaded models, parameter sizes, quantization format, VRAM usage, and model expiration time.
Graceful Degradation: When Ollama is not installed or offline, status reports down or unavailable without degrading device health. Preserves vLLM support on DGX Spark.
Requirement 9 — Remote Sync Monitoring
Decoupled Diagnostics: Extended sync reporting collects pending_changes, failed_batches, conflicts, sync_api_health, and db_health.
Independent Alerting: Sync failures raise SYNC_FAILED, SYNC_CONFLICTS, CENTRAL_API_UNREACHABLE, or DATABASE_UNHEALTHY without marking the device hardware offline.
