5. New APIs and Database Changes
Database Changes
All new tables and schema additions were implemented via programmatic migration (_migrate(conn)) in 

server/fleet_server.py
 to preserve exact compatibility with 

server/schema.sql
 and the baseline schema tests:

device_configs: Stores dynamic configuration overrides (target_type, target_id, version, config_json, updated_at).
device_logs: Stores structured sanitized logs (event_id PRIMARY KEY, device_id, service, category, severity, timestamp, message, attributes, received_at).
sync_reports.details: JSON column for extended sync diagnostics.
New API Endpoints
POST /api/v1/config (Admin Auth): Set remote configuration overrides.
GET /api/v1/config (Admin Auth): List all active configuration overrides.
GET /api/v1/devices/{id}/config (Fleet Token Auth): Fetch effective inherited configuration for a device.
POST /api/v1/logs (Fleet Token Auth): Ingest batches of structured logs with automatic redaction and deduplication.
GET /api/v1/devices/{id}/logs (Dashboard / Admin Auth): Retrieve recent device logs with limit, category, and severity filters.
GET /api/v1/devices/{id}?extended=1: Returns extended sync metrics, log activity states, and effective configuration.
6. Dependencies Added
Zero new external Python packages or message brokers: Relies exclusively on Python's standard library (sqlite3, urllib, re, subprocess, unittest) and existing psutil.
System package on Raspberry Pi OS: libraspberrypi-bin (provides vcgencmd; if omitted, the agent falls back to sysfs thermal zone automatically).
