8. Raspberry Pi 5 Hardware Tests Still Required
When deploying to a physical Raspberry Pi 5 board, the following manual validations should be performed:

Power Supply & Undervoltage: Verify that running on a sub-5A power supply triggers the 0x1 bit in vcgencmd get_throttled and that the server raises THROTTLED_UNDERVOLTAGE.
Thermal Load & Active Cooler: Run stress-ng or cpuburn-aarch64 to verify Active Cooler fan kick-in at 60°C and alert triggering if the CPU exceeds 75°C (warning) or 80°C (critical).
Ollama on Physical Pi 5: Test Ollama token generation with llama3.2:1b or llama3.2:3b on 4GB vs 8GB Raspberry Pi 5 hardware.
Physical Systemd Installation: Validate sudo agent/install-agent.sh on standard Raspberry Pi OS (Debian 12 Bookworm 64-bit).
9. Remaining Risks and Blockers
Third-Party USB-C Chargers: Many standard USB-C chargers drop below 5.0V under Raspberry Pi 5 peak loads (which can draw up to 5A), inducing undervoltage throttling. Documented in the 

README.md
 troubleshooting guide.
Custom Minimal OS Images: On custom Linux distributions where libraspberrypi-bin is unavailable, thermal metrics fall back to sysfs, but throttling bitmasks cannot be queried. The agent handles this cleanly by marking throttling flags as unavailable.
